Optimal Solution - DP solution that computes set bits for all numbers using the relation between i and i/2.
                   Reuse previously computed results: every number’s bit count depends on its half, plus one if it’s odd.

class Solution {
    public int[] countBits(int n) {
        // Array to store number of set bits for all numbers from 0 to n
        int[] res = new int[n + 1];
        // If n is 0, array with single element 0 is already correct
        if (n == 0)
            return res;
        // Base case: number of set bits in 0 is 0
        res[0] = 0;
        // Compute set bits for each number from 1 to n
        for (int i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
            // If i is odd, it has one more set bit than i/2
            if (i % 2 != 0) {
                res[i] = res[i / 2] + 1;
            }
            // If i is even, it has the same number of set bits as i/2
            else {
                res[i] = res[i / 2];
            }
        }
        // Return the result array
        return res;
    }
}

Time Complexity :- O(N).
Space Complexity :- O(N).
